# Argo Monitoring Services Documentation

This rule documents the various monitoring services in the Argo system for reference before potential removal.

## Summary Table

| Service | Type | Location | Status | Interval | Safe to Remove? |
|---------|------|----------|--------|----------|-----------------|
| thermal-monitor | Shell/Systemd | `/usr/local/bin`<br>`/etc/systemd/system` | enabled & active | 30s | ✅ Yes (update lifecycle mgr) |
| memory-monitor | Shell/Systemd | `/usr/local/bin`<br>`/etc/systemd/system` | enabled & active | 30s | ✅ Yes (redundant with psutil) |
| cursor-monitor | Shell/Systemd | `/usr/local/bin`<br>`/etc/systemd/system` | enabled & active | 60s | ✅ Yes (dev/debug tool) |
| orangepi-monitor | Systemd | `/etc/systemd/system` | enabled & active | 5s | ✅ Yes (potentially redundant) |
| argo-storage-monitor | Python/User Systemd | `launch/`<br>User service | enabled & active | On-demand | ✅ Yes (if no GUI needed) |
| memory_monitor.py | Python Tool | `launch/` | Manual only | 10s | ✅ Yes (dev tool) |
| argo_service_monitor.py | ROS2 Node | `launch/` | Manual only | 2s | ✅ Yes (if not needed) |
| argo_file_monitor.py | ROS2 Node | `launch/` | Manual only | N/A | ✅ Yes (dev tool) |
| temp_monitor.py | ROS2 Node | `nodes/` | Auto-launched | 1Hz | ⚠️ **Keep** (core safety) |
| storage_monitor.py | Python CLI | `launch/` | Manual only | On-demand | ⚠️ **Keep** (useful CLI) |

## 1. Thermal Monitoring Service (System-Level)

### Files
- **[launch/thermal-monitor.sh](mdc:launch/thermal-monitor.sh)** - Shell script that logs thermal data
- **[launch/thermal-monitor.service](mdc:launch/thermal-monitor.service)** - Systemd service configuration
- **[docs/README-thermal-monitoring.md](mdc:docs/README-thermal-monitoring.md)** - Installation and usage documentation (see also [launch/README-thermal-monitor.md](mdc:launch/README-thermal-monitor.md) stub)

### Purpose
Monitors Orange Pi Zero 2W thermal zones and logs temperatures every 30 seconds to persistent storage.

### Implementation Details
```bash
# Monitors 4 thermal zones:
thermal_zone0 - GPU temperature
thermal_zone1 - VE (Video Engine) temperature  
thermal_zone2 - CPU temperature
thermal_zone3 - DDR (Memory) temperature

# Log format (daily rotation):
/var/log.hdd/persistent/thermal-YYYYMMDD.log
2025-10-01 06:30:23: GPU:60°C VE:57°C CPU:58°C DDR:58°C

# Alert threshold: >80°C triggers syslog warning
```

### Integration Points
- **argo_lifecycle_manager.py** (lines 824-847): Reads thermal logs for fast CPU temperature retrieval in status checks
- Runs as root systemd service with auto-restart
- Avoids expensive `sensors` command for performance

### Installation
```bash
sudo cp launch/thermal-monitor.sh /usr/local/bin/thermal-monitor.sh
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/thermal-monitor.sh
sudo cp launch/thermal-monitor.service /etc/systemd/system/
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable thermal-monitor.service
sudo systemctl start thermal-monitor.service
```

## 2. Storage Monitoring Service (GUI Notifications)

### Files
- **[launch/argo_storage_notifications.py](mdc:launch/argo_storage_notifications.py)** - Python notification script
- **[launch/argo-storage-monitor.service](mdc:launch/argo-storage-monitor.service)** - Systemd service configuration
- **[launch/storage_monitor.py](mdc:launch/storage_monitor.py)** - CLI storage monitoring tool

### Purpose
Monitors disk space and calculates remaining recording hours, sends GUI notifications for storage warnings.

### Implementation Details
```python
# Recording rate constants
RECORDING_RATE_MB_PER_HOUR = 13.5  # MB per hour
RECORDING_RATE_GB_PER_HOUR = 13.5 / 1024.0

# Notification thresholds
CRITICAL_HOURS = 10.0   # Critical warning below 10 hours
WARNING_HOURS = 24.0    # Warning below 24 hours

# Notification urgency levels:
- Critical: urgency="critical", icon="dialog-error"
- Warning: urgency="normal", icon="dialog-warning"
```

### Integration Points
- Runs as user service (orangepi) in GUI environment
- Requires DISPLAY=:0 and XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1000
- Restart on failure with 5-minute RestartSec
- Depends on graphical.target

### Installation
```bash
sudo systemctl --user link /home/orangepi/argo/launch/argo-storage-monitor.service
sudo systemctl --user daemon-reload
sudo systemctl --user enable argo-storage-monitor.service
sudo systemctl --user start argo-storage-monitor.service
```

## 3. Memory Monitoring (Development Tool)

### Files
- **[launch/memory_monitor.py](mdc:launch/memory_monitor.py)** - Memory leak detection tool

### Purpose
Development tool to monitor system memory and per-node memory usage for leak detection.

### Implementation Details
```python
# Default monitoring parameters
Duration: 30 minutes
Interval: 10 seconds (6 samples per minute)

# Output: CSV file with timestamp
memory_usage_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.csv

# Columns:
- Timestamp
- Total system memory (MB)
- Available memory (MB)
- Per-node RSS memory (MB)
```

### Usage Pattern
```bash
# Background monitoring
nohup python3 launch/memory_monitor.py > memory_monitor.log 2>&1 &

# Monitor specific duration
python3 launch/memory_monitor.py --duration 60 --interval 5
```

### Integration Points
- Uses ArgoNodeManager for dynamic node discovery
- Tracks all discovered ROS2 nodes
- Saves CSV to repo root for analysis
- Not a systemd service (manual execution only)

## 4. Temperature ROS2 Node (Real-time Monitoring)

### Files
- **[nodes/temp_monitor.py](mdc:nodes/temp_monitor.py)** - ROS2 temperature monitoring node

### Purpose
ROS2 node that publishes CPU temperature and system temperature with alert capabilities.

### Implementation Details
```python
# Published Topics
/cpu_temperature (Float32) - CPU temperature in Celsius
/system_temperature (Float32) - Overall system temperature
/temperature_high_alert (Bool) - High temperature warning
/temperature_critical_alert (Bool) - Critical temperature warning

# Alert Thresholds (configurable)
HIGH_TEMPERATURE_THRESHOLD_C = 85.0°C
CRITICAL_TEMPERATURE_THRESHOLD_C = 100.0°C
TEMPERATURE_HYSTERESIS_C = 2.0°C

# Publishing Optimization (saves rosbag space)
- First 30s: Publishes all data at 1Hz
- After 30s: Publishes only on >5% change OR every 60s
- Alert topics: Always 1Hz for safety

# QoS Configuration
- Temperature alerts use TRANSIENT_LOCAL durability
- Late-joining nodes get current alert state
```

### Debug Mode
```bash
# ASCII terminal bars with --debug flag
python3 nodes/temp_monitor.py --debug
```

### Integration Points
- Launched by argo_lifecycle_manager.py
- Part of core ROS2 node ecosystem
- Temperature data recorded in rosbags
- Persistent QoS for critical alerts

