## 7. System Memory Monitoring Service (Shell-based)

### Files
- **/usr/local/bin/memory-monitor.sh** - Comprehensive memory monitoring script
- **/etc/systemd/system/memory-monitor.service** - Systemd service (enabled & active)

### Purpose
System-level memory monitoring that logs memory usage, swap usage, and top memory consumers every 30 seconds.

### Implementation Details
```bash
# Monitoring interval: 30 seconds

# Log files (daily rotation):
/var/log.hdd/persistent/memory-YYYYMMDD.log        # Memory statistics
/var/log.hdd/persistent/processes-YYYYMMDD.log     # Top memory consumers

# Memory log format:
2025-10-01 07:15:23: Memory:73% Swap:0% MemTotal=1982916 MemFree=234156 MemAvailable=524892...

# Process log format:
2025-10-01 07:15:23: Top memory consumers:
[ps aux output sorted by %mem, top 10 processes]

# Alert thresholds:
- Memory >85%: Logs HIGH MEMORY USAGE and sends syslog warning
- Swap >60%: Sends syslog warning
```

### Installation Status
```bash
# Currently installed and running:
sudo systemctl status memory-monitor.service
# ● memory-monitor.service - Memory usage monitoring and logging
#    Loaded: loaded (/etc/systemd/system/memory-monitor.service; enabled)
#    Active: active (running)
```

### Integration Points
- Runs as root systemd service with auto-restart (RestartSec=10)
- Provides historical memory usage data for diagnostics
- Complements Python memory_monitor.py (which focuses on ROS2 nodes)

## 8. Cursor Process Monitoring Service

### Files
- **/usr/local/bin/cursor-monitor.sh** - Cursor IDE process monitoring script
- **/etc/systemd/system/cursor-monitor.service** - Systemd service (enabled & active)

### Purpose
Monitors Cursor IDE processes for resource usage, especially helpful for diagnosing performance issues on resource-constrained Orange Pi.

### Implementation Details
```bash
# Monitoring interval: 60 seconds (every minute)

# Log file (daily rotation):
/var/log.hdd/persistent/cursor-processes-YYYYMMDD.log

# Log format:
2025-10-01 07:15:23: Cursor processes: 5, Total Memory: 450MB
[Full ps aux output for cursor processes]

# Monitored processes:
- cursor.*server
- cursor.*agent  
- cursor.*extension

# Alert threshold:
- Memory >1GB: Sends syslog daemon.warning
```

### Installation Status
```bash
# Currently installed and running:
sudo systemctl status cursor-monitor.service
# ● cursor-monitor.service - Cursor process monitoring
#    Loaded: loaded (/etc/systemd/system/cursor-monitor.service; enabled)
#    Active: active (running)
```

### Integration Points
- Runs as root systemd service with auto-restart (RestartSec=10)
- Helps identify Cursor IDE memory leaks or performance issues
- Particularly useful on 2GB RAM Orange Pi systems

## 9. Orange Pi System Monitor Service

### Files
- **/etc/systemd/system/orangepi-monitor.service** - Systemd service (enabled & active)
- Uses system command: `orangepimonitor -m`

### Purpose
Orange Pi-specific system monitoring using the built-in orangepimonitor utility for CPU stats, load, and temperature.

### Implementation Details
```bash
# Log file (daily rotation):
/var/log.hdd/persistent/orangepi-monitor-YYYYMMDD.log

# Output format (every 5 seconds):
Time        CPU    load %cpu %sys %usr %nice %io %irq   CPU  C.St.
07:17:57:   ---    1.31  11%   2%   9%   0%   0%   0% 56.6°C  0/7

# Metrics:
- System load average
- CPU usage percentage (total, system, user, nice, io, irq)
- CPU temperature
- C-states (power states)
```

### Installation Status
```bash
# Currently installed and running:
sudo systemctl status orangepi-monitor.service
# ● orangepi-monitor.service - Orange Pi Monitor logging service
#    Loaded: loaded (/etc/systemd/system/orangepi-monitor.service; enabled)
#    Active: active (running)
```

### Integration Points
- Runs as root systemd service
- No auto-restart (Restart=no)
- Uses native Orange Pi monitoring tool
- Provides detailed CPU statistics and C-state information

